# PRIMER DESIGN FRAMEWORK TOOL TABLE

This table organizes primer design tools by their role in a modular primer design framework, from sequence input/alignment through candidate generation, specificity filtering, and assay-set optimization.

---

## 🔹 Stage 1 — Input / Alignment

| Tool / implementation | CLI? | Input types | Outputs | Stage fit | Strengths / limitations | Example command snippet |
|----------------------|------|------------|----------|------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| MAFFT | Yes | FASTA sequences | MSA (FASTA/other formats) | Stage 1 | Fast C implementation; auto strategy selection; multithreading support | `mafft --auto input.fasta > aligned.fasta` |
| Clustal Omega (`clustalo`) | Yes | FASTA sequences (3+ sequences) | MSA output file | Stage 1 | Parallelized; widely used; scalable | `clustalo -i input.fasta -o aligned.fasta --threads=8` |

---

## 🔹 Stage 2 — Candidate Generation

| Tool / implementation | CLI? | Input types | Outputs | Stage fit | Strengths / limitations | Example command snippet |
|----------------------|------|------------|----------|------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| Primer3 (`primer3_core`) | Yes | Boulder-IO formatted input + template + constraints | Primer pairs (text output) | Stage 2 | Gold standard; highly configurable; no built-in specificity | `primer3_core < input.txt > output.txt` |
| EMBOSS `eprimer3` | Yes | Sequence input | Primer3-style output | Stage 2 | EMBOSS wrapper around Primer3 | `eprimer3 input.fa output.txt` |
| primer3-py | Yes (Python / scriptable) | Python API with Primer3 parameters | Primer objects + thermo helpers | Stage 2 (+thermo) | Python bindings; good for pipelines; relies on Primer3 core | `import primer3 / primer3.calc_tm(...) / primer3.bindings.design_primers(...)` |
| PMPrimer | Yes | FASTA (aligned or unaligned) | JSON/CSV primer sets | Stage 2–4 | Conserved-region detection; BLAST integration; multiplex support | `pmprimer -f seqs.fasta` |
| primerdiffer | Yes | Two genomes (FASTA) + optional VCF | Discriminatory primer sets | Stage 2–3 | Haplotype discrimination; integrates BLAST | `primerdesign.py -g1 genome1.fa -g2 genome2.fa -pos ...` |
| Primer Prospector | Yes | Aligned FASTA | Primer lists + coverage statistics | Stage 2–3 | Taxonomy-aware; de novo primer discovery | `analyze_primers.py -f targets.fasta -P primers.txt` |
| PUPpy | Yes | ResultDB.tsv + CDS directory | Primer tables + plots | Stage 2 | Community-specific primer design | `puppy-primers -p group` |
| DegePrime | Yes (Perl) | Trimmed alignment FASTA | TSV of degenerate primer windows | Stage 2 | Entropy-based degenerate primer design | `perl DegePrime.pl -i trimmed.fasta -d 12 -l 18 -o out.tsv` |
| HYDEN | Yes | DNA sequences + constraints | Degenerate primer pairs | Stage 2 | Batch CLI program; academic availability |  |
| PrimalScheme | Yes | FASTA references (viral genomes) | Primer BED/TSV + JSON reports | Stage 2–4 | ARTIC-compatible tiling; greedy approach | `primalscheme multiplex input.fasta` |
| Olivar | Yes | MSA or reference FASTA | Primer BED + config files | Stage 2–4 | Tiling + specificity + optimization | `olivar build -m input.fasta -o out` |
| varVAMP | Yes | MSA alignment | Primer schemes | Stage 2–4 | Designed for highly variable viruses | `varvamp tiled alignment.fasta outdir` |
| NGS-PrimerPlex | Yes | BED + reference genome | Multiplex primer panels | Stage 2–4 | Integrates Primer3 + BWA; high-throughput |Setup: `docker pull aakechin/ngs-primerplex:1.3.4` Usage: `python3 NGS_primerplex.py ...` |

