## 🔹 Stage 3 — Expensive Filtering / Specificity / In-Silico PCR

| Tool / implementation | CLI? | Input types | Outputs | Stage fit | Strengths / limitations | Example command snippet |
|----------------------|------|------------|----------|------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| BLAST+ (`makeblastdb`) | Yes | FASTA reference | Local BLAST database | Stage 3 | Custom database preparation | `makeblastdb -in sequences.fasta -dbtype nucl \ -out custom_db -parse_seqids`|
| BLAST+ (`blastn-short`) | Yes | Primer sequences + BLAST DB | Similarity hits | Stage 3 | Optimized for short sequences | `blastn -task blastn-short -word_size 7 -dust no \ -soft_masking false -penalty -3 -reward 1 \ -gapopen 5 -evalue 1000` |
| MFEprimer | Yes | Primer FASTA + indexed DB | QC report (GC/Tm/ΔG/binding counts) | Stage 3 | Thermodynamics-aware QC | `mfeprimer index -i genome.fa` then `mfeprimer -i primers.fa -d genome.fa` |
| ThermonucleotideBLAST (`tntblast`) | Yes | Assay file + DB | Match report | Stage 3 | Thermodynamic specificity search | `tntblast -i query.txt -d db.fa` |
| UCSC `isPcr` | Yes | Genome DB + primer file | Predicted PCR products | Stage 3 | Widely used in-silico PCR | `isPcr genome.2bit primers.txt out.txt` |
| Exonerate `ipcress` | Yes | Primer file + sequences | PCR product predictions | Stage 3 | Faster than e-PCR; ambiguity tolerant | `ipcress primers.txt genome.fa` |
| EMBOSS `primersearch` | Yes | Primer file + FASTA | Amplimer report | Stage 3 | Simple mismatch-tolerant PCR simulation | `primersearch -seqall targets.fa -infile primers.txt` |
| VirtualPCR | Yes | Config file + FASTA | PCR product predictions | Stage 3 | Handles many primers; memory tuning | `java -jar virtualPCR.jar config.file` |

---

## 🔹 Stage 4 — Assay Set Optimization / Pooling

| Tool / implementation | CLI? | Input types | Outputs | Stage fit | Strengths / limitations | Example command snippet |
|----------------------|------|------------|----------|------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| multiPrime | Yes (Snakemake) | Config YAML + FASTA | Minimal primer sets | Stage 4 | Explicit minimal-set optimization | `snakemake --configfile multi.yaml --cores 10` |
| PrimalScheme3 | Yes | MSA + BED | Interaction reports + scheme repair | Stage 3–4 | Dimer interaction detection + repair | `primalscheme3 interactions scheme.bed` |
| SADDLE (via Olivar) | Embedded | Dimer scoring matrix | Optimized tiling panels | Stage 4 | Simulated annealing optimization | `(invoked within Olivar workflow)` |
| openPrimeR | R / scriptable | Template sequences and optionally primer sets; FASTA or CSV inputs are supported in the vignette workflows | Multiplex primer sets; analysis/comparison outputs in R | Stage 4 | Set-cover-based multiplex optimization; also analyzes and compares primer sets; not a standalone Unix binary | `library(openPrimeR)` |
